          This folder contains the following subfolders:

          Folder Name               Description

          <DRIVERARM64>     64-bit ARM target libraries
          <DRIVERINTEL32>   32-bit Intel target libraries
          <DRIVERINTEL64>   64-bit Intel target libraries

          <C_C++>           C and C++ example programs
          <Python>          Python driver and examples

          LICENSE.PDF       License agreement for Linux driver software
          README            This document

          Refer to the end of this document for corrections,
          warnings, and additional information.



     INTRODUCTION

          BTIDriver is a unified Application Programming
          Interface (API) for Ballard Avionics Databus
          Interface PCI, USB, and Ethernet devices.
          These avionics databus interfaces include
          MIL-STD-1553, ARINC 429, ARINC 717, ARINC 708, and
          others.  The <DRIVERINTEL32>, <DRIVERINTEL64>, and
          <DRIVERARM64> folders contain the driver files,
          and the <C_C++> and <Python> folders contain 
          programming files and examples.



     ACCESSING USB DEVICES

          This directory contains drivers that can access PCI,
          USB, and Ethernet devices.  When accessing USB devices,
          these drivers use the USB kernel driver.  See the <BTIKUSB>
          directory for more information.

          Alternatively, USB devices can be access using libusb-1.0.
          See the <BTIDRIVER_LIBUSB1> directory for more information.



     CORRECTIONS, WARNINGS, AND ADDITIONAL INFORMATION

          There is no additional information.


